§ INVARIANTS
  t∞: CSSL source = canonical behavior
  t∞: foreign implementation = oracle/bootstrap debt only
  t∞: GPU-visible resources carry type-domain proof
  t∞: p99 > budget = release blocker
  t∞: CPU reference exists for every new GPU math primitive
  t∞: render richness cannot violate deterministic gameplay
  t∞: telemetry local+consensual; N! surveillance
  t∞: no TODO without owner+gate+phase

§ RISKS
  risk.bootstrap_stasis:
    symptom: Rust/Odin scaffold becomes permanent
    mitigation: banlist + phase gate + replacement owner

  risk.compiler_surface_too_wide:
    symptom: GPU attrs added faster than emitters validate
    mitigation: vertical slices; one kernel→one backend→one test before expansion

  risk.frame_pacing_lies:
    symptom: avg FPS passes while p99 fails
    mitigation: p99/p99.9 gates; timestamp queries; capture overhead isolated

  risk.memory_unsafety:
    symptom: hidden CPU/GPU coherency bugs
    mitigation: gpu<T>/shared<T>/staged<T> enforced by compiler

  risk.visual_without_game:
    symptom: renderer advances, competitive feel absent
    mitigation: P3+P6 simultaneous; input/sim gates active from P1

§ ANTI-PATTERNS
  ✗ port LoA to Odin/wgpu ∵ violates CSSL-only invariant
  ✗ keep v13 CPU DIB renderer as mainline ∵ wastes GPU + blocks high refresh
  ✗ add ad hoc host handles ∵ bypasses Cap/effect safety
  ✗ optimize average FPS ∵ competitive gameplay needs p99/p99.9
  ✗ accept WGSL as source of truth ∵ CSSL compiler must own kernels
