        G = (lit.r*0.48+x_norm*0.20+material_mix*0.16)*(1-object_mask*0.18)+object_mask*material_mix*0.25+edge*0.10
        B = (lit.r*0.30+y_norm*0.20+descriptor_canary*0.12+(1-material_mix)*0.20)*(1-object_mask*0.22)+object_mask*(1-material_mix)*0.25+edge*0.06
      host headless expected-pixel oracle mirrors the object/depth formula
      yaw byte test adjusted: row-byte quantization can hide yaw, so raw ray math + 2D tile bytes now guard yaw response
